From 05615de720f8438503e5da8ac50cbb17e8661b0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/57] hw/misc, hw/dma, hw/timer: SAM D5x DAC and EVSYS; DMAC
 pulsed triggers

The speaker of the PyKit Ruler, played the way CircuitPython's audioio
and synthio drive it:

- mchp-dac (DAC U2502): two channels converting at once, DATABUF at a
  START event when EVCTRL.STARTEIx is set; properties value0/value1 and
  "audio", the output since the previous read as PCM for front ends.
- mchp-evsys-u2504 (EVSYS U2504): asynchronous and synchronous paths,
  EVD/OVR flags, the five interrupt lines; same GPIO names as mchp-evsys
  so the SoC wires its event table to either.
- DMAC: triggers pulsed by a TC overflow (one pending per channel; a run
  for pulses serves only the channels that took one, never a channel
  firmware has just enabled and is about to clear the flags of), and
  block events (CHEVCTRL.EVOE, EVOSEL BLOCK) after the next descriptor
  is fetched. The DMAC tells each TC whether a channel waits for its
  overflow; the TC then serves every overflow, even far behind.
- mchp_event_time_ns(): the virtual time of the event a late timer is
  serving, so the DAC's timeline keeps the spacing of a burst of TC
  overflows.
- Regenerated DAC and EVSYS tables (overlays), curiosity-cp qtest
  (dac-audio), board doc docs/system/arm/curiosity-circuitpython.rst.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted; not for submission to upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
