--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/system/arm/curiosity-circuitpython.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+Microchip Curiosity CircuitPython / PyKit Explorer (``curiosity-circuitpython``)
+================================================================================
+
+.. note::
+   Peripheral Pretender: a personal project in a downstream fork
+   of QEMU. AI-assisted code; not for submission to upstream QEMU.
+
+The Curiosity PyKit Explorer is a CircuitPython kit: the Curiosity
+CircuitPython board (EV78P89A) on the PyKit Ruler baseboard (EV82H04A). The
+controller is an ATSAME51J20A: an Arm Cortex-M4F at up to 120 MHz with
+1 MiB of flash, 256 KiB of SRAM and 8 KiB of backup RAM, here with a
+32.768 kHz crystal and no main crystal.
+
+The SoC model (``atsame51j20a-soc``) is the generic PIC32CM SoC model (see
+:doc:`pic32cm-jh01-cpro`) built from the ATSAME51J20A device description:
+the CPU is ``cortex-m4`` (CPUID 0x410FC241, r0p1, with the FPU), and
+peripherals are QOM children of ``/machine/soc`` named after their instance.
+
+Modelled SAM D5x peripherals
+""""""""""""""""""""""""""""
+
+Besides the PORT, SERCOM (USART, SPI, I2C host), EIC, TC, TCC, RTC, WDT,
+PAC and DSU models shared with the PIC32CM devices:
+
+- OSCCTRL (XOSC0/1, DFLL48M, two FDPLL200M), OSC32KCTRL, MCLK, GCLK (12
+  generators; source numbering of the SAM D5x), NVMCTRL (READY, commands
+  logged), TRNG.
+- QSPI in serial memory mode, with the AHB window at 0x04000000; an SST26VF
+  quad SPI flash behind it.
+- USB device controller with a built-in host: it enumerates the device and
+  opens the first CDC ACM interface (115200 8N1, DTR and RTS), whose data is
+  a QEMU serial port. CircuitPython's REPL appears there. Mass storage,
+  HID, audio and MIDI interfaces are enumerated but not used.
+- DMAC: descriptors, write-back memory, software triggers and peripheral
+  triggers (SERCOM DRE/RXC flags; TC overflows as pulses), block events.
+- EVSYS (U2504): asynchronous and synchronous paths, EVD/OVR flags and the
+  five interrupt lines.
+- ADC (instant conversions; pins from the ``ain`` property, the supply and
+  the temperature sensor), DAC (two channels, START events; the ``audio``
+  property described below).
+
+Board
+"""""
+
+- QSPI flash: SST26VF032B (4 MiB), contents from ``-drive if=mtd,index=0``
+  (a raw image; CircuitPython keeps its CIRCUITPY FAT file system there).
+- Red LED D13 on PB23 (QEMU LED device). USER button on PA27 to ground with
+  a 10 kOhm pull-up: the machine property ``user-pressed``.
+- ``-serial`` options: with ``console=usb`` (default) serial0 is the USB
+  CDC console, serial1 the debug UART (SERCOM3, PA22/PA23), serial2 the
+  RNBD451 BLE module's UART (SERCOM2). ``console=debug`` swaps the first
+  two, for bare-metal test images that print on the debug UART.
+- RNBD451 BLE module (``rnbd451``): command mode (``$$$``), ``V``, ``D``,
+  ``---``, with the replies of the module on the kit; its reset on PA14.
+- The UF2 bootloader occupies the first 16 KiB on the real board. When
+  nothing is loaded at address 0, the machine starts an image linked at
+  0x4000 the way the bootloader does, so CircuitPython's ELF runs as is.
+
+The PyKit Ruler:
+
+- ST7789V 1.14" 240 x 135 TFT on SERCOM0 SPI (PA04/PA05, CS PA07, D/C PB14,
+  backlight PA06 active low). Its picture is ``/machine/lcd``: properties
+  ``frame`` (base64 RGB565) and ``frame-gen``.
+- Five WS2812B NeoPixels in one chain on PB22: ``/machine/neopixels``,
+  property ``pixels`` (``RRGGBB`` per LED) and ``gen``.
+- ICM-20948 IMU (with its AK09916 magnetometer) at I2C address 0x69:
+  ``/machine/imu``, properties ``accel`` (mg, ``"x y z"``), ``gyro``,
+  ``mag``.
+- ``bno085=on`` adds a BNO085 breakout at 0x4A on the QWIIC connector
+  (``/machine/qwiic-bno085``), as on the kit this model was checked against.
+- Speaker: DAC0 (PA02) drives the amplifier. ``/machine/soc/dac`` has
+  ``value0``/``value1`` (12-bit output codes) and ``audio``: each read
+  returns the output since the previous read as ``"<rate> <seq> <base64>"``
+  (signed 16-bit samples at ``audio-rate``, default 22050 Hz, mid-scale
+  0), or an empty string while the output does not change.
+
+Running CircuitPython
+"""""""""""""""""""""
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+  $ qemu-system-arm -M curiosity-circuitpython \
+      -kernel adafruit-circuitpython-microchip_curiosity_circuitpython-10.1.4.elf \
+      -drive if=mtd,format=raw,file=circuitpy.img \
+      -serial stdio -display none -icount shift=auto,sleep=on
+
+The ELF is Adafruit's UF2 converted (``tools/pp/uf2.py`` in Peripheral
+Pretender); ``tools/pp/fatfs.py`` builds and reads the drive image.
